_*.png
_*.txt

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# THE SHELL'S AUDIO IS COMMITTED.
#
# It used to be generated, and that was a mistake. Every developer had to
# install ffmpeg and numpy and run two scripts, each one produced a slightly
# different file, and a fresh clone had NO audio at all - so the app a new
# developer built was not the app anyone else was testing. The files are
# 1.3 MB in total, which is nothing, and committing them is what makes every
# clone identical.
#
# The generators are still here, but they are for CHANGING a sound, not for
# building. They refuse to overwrite a committed file unless you pass
# --force, so nobody can regenerate the audio by accident and ship a
# different one.
#
#     python Tools/_gen_audio.py --force   (sfx_tap / sfx_select / sfx_back / sfx_tick)
#     python Tools/_gen_bgm.py --force     (bgm_shell, seamless loop)
#
# The .wav intermediates are still ignored - they are scratch.
app/src/main/res/raw/*.wav

# Raw puzzle source dump (2.7 MB Lichess export). The runtime asset
# games/chess/puzzles.js IS committed; regenerate it with:
#     python Tools/_gen_puzzles.py
sources/LockedGames/chess_puzzles.txt
# One-off debugging scratch from device sessions (the committed tooling is
# Tools/_gen_puzzles.py / Tools/_install_chess.py / Tools/_validate_chess.js /
# Tools/_check_chess_syntax.js)
_cd*.js
_pm_probe.py
_fix_pm.py
_u*.xml
